### Remaining Concerns (your call)
1. **The Bruce Miller "left or right" thread is raised, re-pointed-at, and never resolved.** The diagnosis says something in her process is illegible and three years isn't enough to say what; the rabbit hole points back at it; the close doesn't touch it. That's deliberate honesty about a medium-confidence read, but it is a genuinely open loop. Leaving it open is defensible — just know it's the one thread the piece doesn't land.
2. **The Academy section ends one beat behind its own climax.** The Emmy resolves the section, then the Oscar-ceremony anecdote follows as a coda that reverts to the deflection theme. I left it because it feeds the name echo into the next H2, but if you'd rather the section land on the Emmy, that paragraph is the one to move or cut.
